hl.lore.ambience=§lSounds§r\n\nFootsteps behind you, doors, chests, distant mining, the hiss of a creeper that isn't there, breathing, nails on the wall, knocking, your name whispered.\n\n§eTip:§r don't turn around. Or do.
hl.lore.gamer=§lHerobrineGamer788§r\n§8(a player who shouldn't be here)§r\n\nHe joins your world like anyone else, wearing a headset whose red light never blinks. He plays, copies you, turns strange and in the end stops pretending.\n\n§eTip:§r when he reveals himself, look on the ground where he stood.
hl.lore.dweller=§lThe Cave Dweller§r\n§8(inspired by Cave Dweller / From The Caves)§r\n\nA pale, eyeless body hunched over, knuckle-walking like something that used to walk upright. Its four-lipped snout opens like a flower over rings of teeth. It flees if you catch it looking; wait too long and it comes for you.\n\n§eTip:§r the flashlight drives it off. Live through it and it leaves something behind.
hl.lore.herobrine=§lHerobrine§r\n§8(the old legend)§r\n\nThree blocks tall, his stomach open and stitched, his ribs splayed like fingers, half his face burned to the bone, his jaw hanging to his chest. His spine comes out of his back and drags behind him like a tail of bone, and splinters of bone grow out of his shoulders and head. He watches from afar and vanishes if you look.\n\n§eTip:§r stare him down three times. Don't hit him.
hl.lore.fog=§lThe Man From The Fog§r\n§8(inspired by The Man From The Fog)§r\n\nOver three blocks of grey, starved body in a soaked yellow slicker down to his ankles and a pulled-down sou'wester. Inside the hood, two white points and a grin from ear to ear. He comes closer when you don't look. At night he knocks on your door.\n\n§eTip:§r live through a fog in which you saw him.
hl.lore.null=§lnull§r\n§8(inspired by The Broken Script)§r\n\nA player the game can't draw: black, torn into slices that don't line up, fringed red and blue, two white eyes and the F3+B box round it. It writes in the chat, corrupts blocks, pretends the game has frozen.\n\n§eTip:§r look it in the eye. Twice.
hl.lore.e303=§lEntity 303§r\n§8(the hacker who never left)§r\n\nA white robe, its hood running to a point and coming apart in strips, red eyes, a mask with a stitched grin. He joins your game, writes in the chat, swaps what you're holding, kicks you (or pretends to). In person he floats, raises his hands and your world is his: you fly, you're teleported, lightning falls. Then he bans you.\n\n§eTip:§r sit through his show. In the end he leaves something.
hl.lore.redNight=§lThe Red Night§r\n\nEvery four days, a night of red fog when everything comes twice as often and your lanterns may go out. It ends at dawn.
hl.lore.boss=§l§4The Hollow Miner§r\n§8(Herobrine, in his true form)§r\n\nNearly five blocks of cracked deepslate with lava inside, his miner's helmet with the lamp still lit, a pickaxe for a right hand, a fist of stone, and his spine raised like a mast over his back, a miner's lamp hanging from the tip. He teleports, calls down lightning, summons Dwellers, puts out the light and stings. At half health he flies into a rage.\n\n§eTip:§r flashlight light burns him.
hl.page.1.title=I. The Player
hl.page.1.text=§oDay 3. A player joined my world. His name was HerobrineGamer788. He wore a headset with a red light. He gave me bread.\n\nDay 4. Today he copied my every step. Every block I mined, he mined.\n\nDay 5. The light on his headset doesn't blink. Neither does he.
hl.page.2.title=II. What Lives Below
hl.page.2.text=§oThere's something in the mine that copies my footsteps. It has no eyes. It doesn't need them.\n\nWhen it opens its mouth, its whole face opens.\n\nIt hates light. I'm running out of batteries.
hl.page.3.title=III. White Eyes
hl.page.3.text=§oI found his pickaxe buried in his own shoulder. He was a miner. He dug too deep, where the stone breathes, and something came back up with him.\n\nNow his eyes are white and his spine is outside his body, dragging behind him like a tail.
hl.page.4.title=IV. The Fog
hl.page.4.text=§oThe fog isn't fog. It's him, waiting, hood up, with that grin.\n\nIf you look at him, he leaves. If you don't, he comes closer.\n\nHe knocked on my door three times. The fourth time he didn't knock.
hl.page.5.title=V. The Error
hl.page.5.text=§oBlocks break into magenta and black. The world comes apart where he walks.\n\nThere's another one. He says he's an admin. He bans me every night and every morning I'm still here.
hl.page.6.title=VI. The Grave
hl.page.6.text=§oA bell rang behind me at night. I went to look: freshly dug earth, a headstone, a black rose. And on the stone, my name.\n\nI went closer. Something was knocking from underneath, slowly, like someone at a door.\n\nI think it wanted out. Or it wanted me in.
hl.page.7.title=VII. The Name
hl.page.7.text=§oThey all serve him. The one in the mine, the one with the tail of bone.\n\nIf you gather these seven pages, call him by his name at night, under the sky. He will come in his true form, and only then can he be hurt.\n\nI can't any more. I don't think I'm the one playing now.
hl.threat.scares=Scares
hl.lore.scares=§lScares§r\n\nNot a creature: the moments when something is too close. A face right in front of yours for the length of a blink. Breath on the back of your neck and something brushing past. A door slamming in an empty house. The screen tearing into static. A blow that hurts and leaves no mark. Your name, written across your eyes.
hl.arrive.scares=§8[???]§r §7Don't blink. Don't turn round. Don't look behind the door.
hl.scare.neck=§7§oSomething brushed the back of your neck.
hl.scare.name_sub=§8i'm watching you
hl.threat.ancient=The Ancient City
hl.lore.ancient=§lThe Ancient City§r\n\nFar below, under the deepslate, there is a city where nobody makes a sound. When you walk in, the game tells you where you are. Inside, the city is awake: candles go out by themselves, shriekers scream with nothing near, your footsteps come back a moment late, the dark pulses like a heart, the portal frame hums and there are whispers. And stay a minute and someone watches you from the ruins.\n\n§eTip:§r don't run, don't make noise and don't stay.
hl.arrive.ancient=§8[???]§r §7Under the deepslate there is a city. Down there, nobody makes a sound.
